# An eleventh Russian story: Tom's first week in Petersburg
subtitle: "Tom's first week in Petersburg, in a sixteen-line letter home: the move, the flat, a neighbour, the kitchen, the way to work and two new chairs. Read it, hear it, then test yourself by eye and by ear."
tags: ["russian","russian reading","russian story","petersburg","russian letter"]
teaches: ["reading/reading-stories","grammar/plural-cases"]
thumb: "band \"An eleventh Russian story\" note \"a letter home\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"All six cases in Russian: one table","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/111-russian-case-table.cast"}

## An eleventh Russian story: Tom's first week in Petersburg
stress: all
level: basic
